  "result": "The rule and its witnesses for NRS_484B_450_1g pass the gate: it returned **OK** on the first run (1 of 6 used), with 14 witnesses.\n\n**The rule**\n- **When it applies (s9, s10):** the subject is a vehicle in a travel region that a traffic signal controls, either directly or through the intersection the lane enters. The signal head must also be:\n  - ahead of the vehicle along the lane's direction;\n  - within 30 ft of the vehicle's front. I wrote this as 4·|head − position|² ≤ (30 ft + 30 ft + length)². Doubling instead of halving the length keeps 30 ft as the only figure in the rule.\n  - beyond a road edge on that edge's side.\n- **The duty:** the vehicle is not at rest, unless one of these holds:\n  - another road user is ahead in the same lane, no more than `p.queue_halt_gap` away;\n  - a device governing a region the vehicle occupies directs a halt: a stop sign, a yield sign, a red signal (circular red, any red arrow, flashing red), a level-crossing signal with lights flashing, or a gate lowering or down;\n  - a police officer governing that region directs it to stop.\n\n**Choices the node left open**\n- **Two exceptions written once:** \"in compliance with law\" names only devices that \"official traffic-control device\" already covers, so I wrote the two together. A second copy could never change a verdict.\n- **Red arrow:** a red arrow in any direction counts, since the record doesn't name one.\n- **Gap to the vehicle ahead:** measured as the straight distance between the two bodies, as the gap's definition says.\n- **No narrowings declared.**\n\n**Extra witnesses:** besides the planned scenarios, I added six so that every condition in the rule is tested:\n- **Compliant:** a stop sign, a yield sign, level-crossing lights flashing, and a gate down.\n- **Violated:** a signal that governs only the intersection, and a signal head beyond the left road edge.\n\nThe run's record is in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
